      "grouping_at_time": "Subpart D \u2014 Design and Construction",
      "title_at_revision": "Control system locks.",
      "text": "If there is a device to lock the control system with the rotorcraft on the ground or water, there must be means to--\n(a) Automatically disengage the lock when the pilot operates the controls in a normal manner, or limit the operation of the rotorcraft so as to give unmistakable warning to the pilot before takeoff; and\n(b) Prevent the lock from engaging in flight.",
